{
  "info": {
    "name": "Experia360 Payment Webhooks API",
    "description": "Every endpoint of the assessment API, with synthetic data only.\n\n1. Start the API (`npm run dev`) and seed it (`npm run seed`).\n2. Create a Postman **environment** with `demoPassword` (SEED_DEMO_PASSWORD) and `webhookSecret` (PROVIDER_WEBHOOK_SECRET) from your .env. Keep them out of this file.\n3. Run the folders in order. Logins store tokens; \"Create payment\" stores the payment id and reference used later.\n\nThe webhook requests sign the raw body in a pre-request script (CryptoJS HMAC-SHA256, hex), exactly as the provider would.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:4000"
    },
